{"path":"README.md","result":"     1	# exposed
     2	
     3	Where do MPs get their money from?
     4	
     5	Imports everyone who has served in the Commons during the configured Parliament and their available declarations into PostgreSQL. Declarations store parsed fields and extracted funding for later display.
     6	
     7	The planned journalist-facing research application is described in the
     8	[backend product specification](docs/specs/journalist-research-backend.md).
     9	
    10	## Getting started
    11	
    12	Requires Python **3.14+**, Docker Compose, a Rust toolchain and
    13	[SQLx CLI](https://github.com/launchbadge/sqlx/tree/v0.9.0/sqlx-cli) **0.9.0**
    14	(matching the Rust workspace). Install the PostgreSQL CLI with:
    15	
    16	```sh
    17	cargo install sqlx-cli --version 0.9.0 --no-default-features --features rustls,postgres,sqlx-toml
    18	```
    19	
    20	Run commands from the repository root:
    21	
    22	```sh
    23	python3.14 -m venv ingest/.venv
    24	ingest/.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r ingest/requirements.lock
    25	ingest/.venv/bin/python -m pip install --no-deps -e ./ingest
    26	```
    27	
    28	Setup cr…1979 tokens truncated…  169	To run the frontend on the host instead of Docker, use Node.js **24+**:
   170	
   171	```sh
   172	cd frontend
   173	npm ci
   174	npm run dev
   175	```
   176	
   177	The host dev server proxies to `http://127.0.0.1:6999` by default. Override
   178	`EXPOSED_API_ORIGIN` when starting Vite to use another backend. This setting is
   179	server-side; the browser always uses the same-origin `/api/search` path.
   180	The frontend image is for local development. `npm run build` produces static
   181	assets in `frontend/dist`; a production host must also route `/api/search` to
   182	the Rust API.
   183	
   184	The similarity threshold slider refreshes results automatically: lower values
   185	include broader matches, from 0 to 1 in steps of 0.01 (default 1). The search URL
   186	preserves the query and threshold, for example `/?q=John&strictness=0.65`.
   187	Search delay, result limits and defaults live in
   188	[`frontend/src/lib/search.ts`](frontend/src/lib/search.ts). The API caps each entity type separately, so the UI describes the returned
   189	results without claiming a total count or offering unsupported pagination.
   190	This slice displays results; entity pages and in-app feedback collection are
   191	future work. Feedback is gathered through manual testing.
   192	
   193	For frontend checks, install dependencies and the browser once, then run:
   194	
   195	```sh
   196	npm --prefix frontend ci
   197	cd frontend && PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=0 npx playwright install chromium && cd ..
   198	make frontend-check
   199	```
   200	
   201	Browser tests use a controlled API to check ranking, request cancellation,
   202	empty/error recovery, text escaping and narrow layouts. For manual verification,
   203	try an MP's name, `HSBC`, a misspelling, clearing a pending query, and stopping
   204	the API to check retry behavior. See the
   205	[search design brief](docs/design/entity-search.md) for the agreed scope.
   206	
   207	## View example declarations from the API
   208	
   209	These standalone scripts require `bash`, `curl` and `jq`; no database, API key or
   210	Python setup is needed. Run from the repository root:
   211	
   212	```sh
   213	./scripts/view-individual-declaration.sh
   214	./scripts/view-legal-entity-declaration.sh
   215	# View the complete API response, including all returned fields and versions:
   216	./scripts/view-individual-declaration.sh --raw
   217	./scripts/view-legal-entity-declaration.sh --raw
   218	```
   219	
   220	The scripts fetch fixed examples directly from Parliament on each run and print
   221	formatted JSON. The default view selects the version with the latest register
   222	publication date and includes the MP, donor, donor status, amount, currency,
   223	company number and how the support was received. Amounts remain decimal strings.
   224	
   225	Examples verified on 20 September 2026:
   226	
   227	| Script | Declaration | Source donor status | Support |
   228	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   229	| Individual | [16901](https://interests-api.parliament.uk/api/v2/Interests/16901), Alex Burghart | Individual | David Robert Meller, GBP 2,000 |
   230	| Legal entity | [16863](https://interests-api.parliament.uk/api/v2/Interests/16863), Dr Simon Opher | Company | Labour Together Limited (09630980), GBP 5,000 |
   231	
   232	Both examples record support linked to the MP but received by a party organisation,
   233	rather than a direct personal payment. The legal-entity example uses the API's
   234	explicit `Company` status. These are illustrative records, not searches for every
   235	individual or legal entity. Upstream records can change; the default view fails
   236	if the expected donor status changes, and `--raw` lets you inspect the response.
   237	
   238	Contains Parliamentary information licensed under the
   239	[Open Parliament Licence v3.0](https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/copyright-parliament/open-parliament-licence/).
   240	
   241	## Useful commands
   242	
   243	| Command | Purpose |
   244	| --- | --- |
   245	| `make db-migrate` | Apply the development schema baseline |
   246	| `make db-revert` | Revert the baseline, deleting its tables and data |
   247	| `make db-migration-status` | Show SQLx migration status |
   248	| `make db-nuke` | Delete the configured database and recreate it from the baseline |
   249	| `make import-members` | Refresh member data |
   250	| `make import-declarations` | Refresh declarations for the stored member cohort |
   251	| `make verify` | Check data in the local Compose database |
   252	| `make check` | Run importer lint, formatting checks, type checks and tests |
   253	| `make frontend-dev` | Start the Svelte frontend and API with live reload |
   254	| `make frontend-check` | Check, build and browser-test the frontend |
   255	| `make test-unit` | Run tests without PostgreSQL |
   256	| `make format` | Format Python files |
   257	| `make db-stop` | Stop local PostgreSQL while retaining data |
   258	
   259	`make test` and `make check` require local PostgreSQL (`make db-start`). Tests create and remove their own temporary databases. Override `EXPOSED_TEST_ADMIN_DSN` with a PostgreSQL URL to use a different test server; it must allow database creation. `SQLX` can also be overridden with an absolute SQLx CLI executable path.
   260	
   261	See the [importer documentation](ingest/README.md) for configuration, data rules and refresh behavior.
